================================================================================
EXTERNAL DEPENDENCIES
================================================================================

Binnacle bundles no third-party code. It contains no vendored libraries, no
compiled binaries, and no downloaded artifacts. Everything in this repository
is original work under the MIT license above.

It invokes the following programs from the host system at runtime. Each is used
through its documented command-line interface only; none is redistributed here,
and each remains under its own license as installed by your distribution.

REQUIRED
  bash            GNU Bash                          GPL-3.0-or-later
                  Runs binnacle-collect.
  grep            GNU grep                          GPL-3.0-or-later
                  Reads cgroup cpu.stat counters in a single pass.
  df              GNU coreutils                     GPL-3.0-or-later
                  Filesystem capacity, behind a 300 s cache.

OPTIONAL — absent without error
  lspci           pciutils                          GPL-2.0-or-later
                  Human-readable GPU names, once at startup. Without it,
                  GPUs fall back to generic vendor labels.
  nvidia-smi      NVIDIA proprietary driver         NVIDIA license
                  NVIDIA utilisation, temperature and VRAM. Without it, no
                  discrete-GPU instrument is created. Run as a long-lived
                  poller only where the card reports no runtime-D3 support;
                  on cards that can runtime-suspend, a slower one-shot poll
                  is used instead so the GPU is not held awake.
  btop            btop++                            Apache-2.0
                  Launched by the "Open btop" button, if installed.

PLATFORM INTERFACES
  Read-only, via the kernel's stable interfaces:
    /proc/stat, /proc/meminfo, /proc/net/route, /proc/<pid>/stat,
    /proc/<pid>/comm, /proc/mounts
    /sys/class/hwmon, /sys/class/drm, /sys/class/net, /sys/block
    /sys/fs/cgroup (cgroup v2 unified hierarchy, cpu controller)

  Qt 6 / QtQuick, Quickshell, and the Omarchy shell's own QML modules
  (qs.Commons, qs.Ui) are runtime hosts provided by the platform, not
  redistributed here.

Binnacle requires no elevated privileges, installs no sudoers policy, opens no
network connections, and writes no files outside its own plugin directory.
